    <bpmn:process id="W_W1184" name="W1184. Influencer &amp; Home Improvement Content Creator Partnership Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Marketing identifies influencer for partnership; or influencer reaches out; or campaign planning cycle
Frequency: ~20–30 active influencer partnerships at any time; ~5–10 new partnerships onboarded per quarter
Volume: ~50–80 sponsored content pieces/month across all partnerships; mix of YouTube, TikTok, Facebook, and Instagram
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager
Participants: Digital Marketing Manager, Content Creator/Influencer, Category Manager, Social Media Specialist, Legal, Finance
Source: workflow W1184 — Influencer &amp; Home Improvement Content Creator Partnership Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1184_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1184_Lane1" name="Social Media Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1184_Lane2" name="Digital Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1184_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1184_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1184_Start5" name="Marketing identifies influencer for partnership; or influencer reaches out; or campaign…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1184_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1184_Task6" name="Influencer identification &amp; vetting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Influencer identification &amp; vetting: (a) Social Media Specialist monitors home improvement content on YouTube, TikTok, Facebook, and Instagram for potential partners; (b) evaluate candidates: (i) audience size (YouTube: &gt; 10,000 subscribers; TikTok: &gt; 50,000 followers; Facebook: &gt; 20,000 page likes), (ii) audience demographics (homeowners, DIYers, contractors within BuildRight&#x27;s geographic coverage), (iii) engagement rate (comments, shares, saves — not just likes), (iv) content quality and brand alignment, (v) audience authenticity (no purchased followers), (vi) previous brand partnerships; (c) create shortlist of 5–10 candidates per quarter for outreach
Responsible (R): Social Media Specialist
Accountable (A): Digital Marketing Manager
Duration: 8 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1184_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1184_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1184_Task7" name="Partnership negotiation &amp; onboarding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Partnership negotiation &amp; onboarding: (a) Digital Marketing Manager contacts selected influencers; discusses partnership scope: content deliverables, timeline, exclusivity (no competing home improvement retailers), compensation; (b) compensation models: (i) flat fee per content piece (YouTube: PHP 15,000–100,000; TikTok: PHP 5,000–30,000; Facebook: PHP 5,000–20,000 depending on following), (ii) affiliate commission (2–5% of sales via unique promo code), (iii) product seeding (free materials/tools for content creation), (iv) hybrid (reduced fee + commission); (c) Legal prepares Influencer Agreement per W62: deliverables, IP rights, disclosure requirements, exclusivity, termination, RA 10173 consent; (d) onboard influencer: provide brand guidelines, product catalog, store locations, unique promo code, and affiliate tracking link
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1–2 weeks/partnership</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1184_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1184_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1184_Task8" name="Content brief &amp; creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Content brief &amp; creation: (a) Digital Marketing Manager provides content brief per campaign: (i) key message and featured products/category, (ii) target audience, (iii) required call-to-action (visit store, use promo code, download app), (iv) mandatory disclosures (&quot;Sponsored by BuildRight&quot; or &quot;#ad&quot;), (v) content format and length guidelines; (b) allow creative freedom — influencers know their audience best; avoid overly scripted content that feels inauthentic; (c) for store-based content: coordinate with Store Manager for filming permission; (d) for product demonstrations: ensure safety protocols per W695 are followed during filming
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Influencer
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1184_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1184_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1184_Task9" name="Content review and approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Content review and approval: (a) influencer submits draft content for review; (b) Digital Marketing Manager reviews for: (i) factual accuracy of product information, (ii) brand safety (no controversial content), (iii) disclosure compliance, (iv) visual quality standards; (c) provide feedback within 48 hours; (d) approved content published per agreed schedule; (e) for unapproved modifications after review: contract remedy per W62 agreement
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Influencer
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 30–60 min/content piece</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1184_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1184_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1184_Task10" name="Performance tracking &amp; payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Performance tracking &amp; payment: (a) track content performance metrics: views, engagement rate, click-through rate, promo code redemptions, attributable sales via affiliate link; (b) for affiliate commission model: system tracks promo code usage per W13 promotions engine; calculate commission monthly; (c) process influencer payment per W62 agreement terms (flat fee: upon publication; commission: monthly); (d) Finance processes payment as marketing expense per W489 budget
Responsible (R): System / Digital Marketing Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1184_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1184_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1184_Task11" name="Partnership review &amp; optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Partnership review &amp; optimization: (a) monthly: review active partnership performance — content ROI (attributable sales ÷ partnership cost); (b) quarterly: decide partnership renewal/termination; (c) top performers: offer longer-term contracts and increased scope; (d) underperformers: provide optimization guidance or terminate per contract terms; (e) annual: compile influencer marketing ROI for marketing budget planning per W677
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1184_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1184_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1184_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1184_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1184_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-282 (ensure controlled execution — Digital Marketing &amp; Social Media (PA-14.2).) | - operational: Digital Marketing Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1184_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1184_Annotation13" targetRef="W1184_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
