    <bpmn:process id="W_W1444" name="W1444. Store-Level Grand Opening Digital Marketing Campaign, Community Outreach &amp; Social Media Amplification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store opening confirmed (target date set per W702); typically triggered 8 weeks before opening
Frequency: 10–15 new store openings per year (per BuildRight&#x27;s expansion plan)
Volume: Each grand opening campaign runs for 8 weeks (4 weeks pre-opening + 4 weeks post-opening); reaches 50,000–200,000 people in the local community depending on market size
Owner: Marketing Campaign Manager
Participants: Marketing Campaign Manager, Digital Marketing Manager, Store Manager (designated), Regional Manager, VP Store Operations, External Media Agency, Local LGU Liaison
Source: workflow W1444 — Store-Level Grand Opening Digital Marketing Campaign, Community Outreach &amp; Social Media Amplification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1444_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1444_Lane1" name="Marketing Campaign Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1444_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1444_Lane3" name="Digital Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1444_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1444_Start5" name="New store opening confirmed (target date set per W702); typically triggered 8 weeks…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1444_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1444_Task6" name="Pre-opening digital campaign planning (T-8 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-opening digital campaign planning (T-8 weeks): Marketing Campaign Manager develops grand opening campaign plan: (a) geo-targeting: define catchment area (30-minute drive time radius around new store), (b) audience segments: (i) DIY homeowners, (ii) trade professionals/contractors, (iii) corporate/institutional buyers, (iv) local government officials, (c) channel mix: (i) Facebook/Instagram ads (geo-targeted to catchment area), (ii) Google Ads (search for &quot;hardware store [city name]&quot;), (iii) TikTok (home improvement content creators in the region), (iv) local radio/TV digital extensions, (d) budget allocation: PHP 300–500K per store opening (adjustable for market size)
Responsible (R): Marketing Campaign Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1444_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1444_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1444_Task7" name="Community and LGU outreach (T-6 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Community and LGU outreach (T-6 weeks): Store Manager and Marketing coordinate: (a) visit local barangay captains and LGU officials — present BuildRight as community partner, (b) arrange pre-opening community events: (i) free DIY workshop (painting basics, simple electrical), (ii) contractor networking breakfast, (iii) job fair for store hiring, (c) secure LGU support for opening day (traffic management, local media coverage), (d) identify local influencer partners (home improvement vloggers, community Facebook group admins) for amplified reach
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Marketing
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1444_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1444_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1444_Task8" name="Digital content production (T-4 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Digital content production (T-4 weeks): Digital Marketing Manager produces: (a) &quot;Coming Soon&quot; video for social media — store exterior, key departments, special features, (b) behind-the-scenes construction progress posts (weekly updates on social media), (c) staff introduction posts (&quot;Meet your BuildRight [city] team&quot;), (d) product teaser posts (&quot;What&#x27;s coming to [city]? Biggest tile selection in the region!&quot;), (e) countdown posts starting T-2 weeks, (f) event page creation on Facebook with opening day details and exclusive promotions
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Campaign Manager
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1444_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1444_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1444_Task9" name="Opening day execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Opening day execution: (a) live social media coverage: Facebook/Instagram Stories, TikTok livestream of ribbon-cutting and store tour, (b) encourage customer-generated content: &quot;First 100 customers get a free BuildRight tote bag — post a photo with #BuildRight[City] for a chance to win PHP 5,000 gift card&quot;, (c) loyalty sign-up drive: dedicated station with tablets for instant registration, (d) trade professional onboarding: Trade Account Manager processes on-the-spot trade account applications, (e) Store Manager and staff engage with every customer — first impression is critical
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Marketing Team
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1444_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1444_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1444_Task10" name="Post-opening digital amplification (T+1 to T+4 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-opening digital amplification (T+1 to T+4 weeks): (a) share customer testimonials and photos on social media, (b) &quot;Thank you [City]&quot; post with opening day statistics (customers served, loyalty members signed up), (c) retarget opening day visitors with follow-up promotions (&quot;Come back this weekend for exclusive deals&quot;), (d) run &quot;Review Us&quot; campaign — incentivize Google/Facebook reviews from opening day customers, (e) monthly performance review for new store: foot traffic, sales, loyalty member activity, digital campaign ROI
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1444_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1444_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1444_Task11" name="Campaign performance review (T+4 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Campaign performance review (T+4 weeks): Marketing Campaign Manager compiles grand opening campaign report: (a) total reach and impressions across all digital channels, (b) foot traffic estimate (opening day and first month), (c) loyalty sign-ups (target: 500+), (d) cost per acquisition (campaign spend ÷ new loyalty members), (e) social media engagement metrics, (f) first-month sales vs. plan, (g) lessons learned for next store opening; build playbook of best practices
Responsible (R): Marketing Campaign Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1444_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1444_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1444_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1444_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1444_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-282 (ensure controlled execution — Digital Marketing &amp; Social Media (PA-14.2).) | - operational: Marketing Campaign Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Marketing Campaign Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1444_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1444_Annotation13" targetRef="W1444_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1444_Flow15" sourceRef="W1444_Start5" targetRef="W1444_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1444_Flow16" sourceRef="W1444_Task6" targetRef="W1444_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1444_Flow17" sourceRef="W1444_Task7" targetRef="W1444_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1444_Flow18" sourceRef="W1444_Task8" targetRef="W1444_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1444_Flow19" sourceRef="W1444_Task9" targetRef="W1444_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1444_Flow20" sourceRef="W1444_Task10" targetRef="W1444_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1444_Flow21" sourceRef="W1444_Task11" targetRef="W1444_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
