    <bpmn:process id="W_W1558" name="W1558. Builder &amp; Contractor Social Media Influencer Partnership Program, Content Co-Creation &amp; Performance Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly influencer program review; or new influencer identified through social media monitoring; or vendor co-marketing opportunity requiring influencer collaboration
Frequency: Ongoing program management; ~20–30 active influencer partnerships; quarterly program review; monthly content production cycles
Volume: ~20–30 active influencer partnerships (YouTube, Facebook, TikTok builders/contractors); ~60–90 content pieces/year; ~PHP 5–10M annual influencer marketing budget
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager
Participants: Digital Marketing Manager, Content Creator, Category Manager, VP Marketing, Influencer/Content Creator, Finance (budget tracking)
Source: workflow W1558 — Builder &amp; Contractor Social Media Influencer Partnership Program, Content Co-Creation &amp; Performance Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1558_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1558_Lane1" name="Digital Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1558_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1558_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1558_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1558_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1558_Lane2" name="Influencer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1558_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1558_Lane3" name="VP Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1558_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1558_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1558_Start5" name="Quarterly influencer program review; or new influencer identified through social media…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1558_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1558_Task6" name="Influencer identification &amp; vetting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Influencer identification &amp; vetting: Digital Marketing Manager identifies potential influencer partners: (a) criteria: (i) audience size: 10,000+ followers on YouTube, Facebook, or TikTok, (ii) audience relevance: &gt; 60% of followers must be in construction, home improvement, or DIY segments, (iii) content quality: professional production value, accurate technical information, positive brand sentiment, (iv) engagement rate: &gt; 3% average engagement (likes + comments ÷ followers), (v) geography: Philippines-based with primarily Filipino audience; (b) vetting: review last 20 posts/videos for brand safety (no offensive content, competitor endorsements, or false product claims); (c) classify influencers: (i) Macro (100K+ followers): 3–5 partnerships for brand awareness campaigns, (ii) Mid-tier (20K–100K): 10–15 partnerships for product-focused content, (iii) Micro (10K–20K): 5–10 partnerships for niche category content (e.g., tile setting specialists, electrical wiring experts)
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1558_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1558_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1558_Task7" name="Partnership onboarding &amp; agreement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Partnership onboarding &amp; agreement: For approved influencers: (a) Digital Marketing Manager negotiates partnership terms: (i) compensation: flat fee per content piece (PHP 10K–50K for mid-tier; PHP 50K–200K for macro), or product-for-content exchange (free tools/materials in exchange for honest review), or affiliate commission (5–8% of sales driven through unique promo code); (ii) content requirements: minimum 1 content piece per quarter featuring BuildRight products, BuildRight store tag or mention, disclosure of partnership per Philippine advertising guidelines; (iii) exclusivity: influencer cannot promote direct competitors (competing hardware/home improvement retailers) during partnership period; (b) Legal Counsel reviews influencer agreement per RA 10173 (data privacy for any audience data sharing) and advertising disclosure requirements
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2–3 hours per partnership</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1558_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1558_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1558_Task8" name="Content co-creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Content co-creation: Quarterly content calendar: (a) Digital Marketing Manager briefs each influencer on quarterly merchandise focus and promotions: (i) Q1: paint and renovation tools — &quot;New Year, New Home&quot; theme, (ii) Q2: summer projects and garden — &quot;Summer Ready&quot; theme, (iii) Q3: waterproofing and emergency repairs — &quot;Rainy Season Prep&quot; theme, (iv) Q4: holiday lighting and home décor — &quot;Holiday Home&quot; theme; (b) influencer produces content featuring BuildRight products in real project contexts: (i) YouTube video: full project build using materials from BuildRight (e.g., &quot;I built a bathroom from scratch — all materials from BuildRight&quot;), (ii) Facebook/Instagram Reel: quick tool review or tip (e.g., &quot;5 things you need from BuildRight before starting your plumbing project&quot;), (iii) TikTok: short-form DIY tip with BuildRight product demo; (c) Content Creator provides BuildRight brand assets, product information, and any specific promotional offers; (d) all content reviewed by Digital Marketing Manager before posting for accuracy and brand alignment
Responsible (R): Influencer / Content Creator / Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter per influencer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1558_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1558_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1558_Task9" name="Performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Performance tracking: Digital Marketing Manager tracks influencer content performance: (a) per content piece: (i) reach and impressions, (ii) engagement rate, (iii) click-through to buildright.com.ph (via UTM tracking links), (iv) promo code redemptions (affiliate model), (v) store traffic attribution (geo-targeted promotions); (b) monthly: aggregate influencer program ROI = (revenue attributed to influencer content + equivalent media value of organic reach) ÷ program cost; (c) quarterly: compare influencer channel performance vs. paid social media advertising vs. email marketing per W1350 — optimize budget allocation based on cost-per-acquisition by channel
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Data Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1558_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1558_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1558_Task10" name="Quarterly program review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly program review: VP Marketing reviews influencer program quarterly: (a) active partnerships and content output; (b) ROI by influencer tier and content type; (c) audience overlap analysis (are multiple influencers reaching the same audience?); (d) renew, renegotiate, or terminate partnerships based on performance; (e) identify new influencer opportunities for underperforming categories; (f) adjust budget allocation for next quarter
Responsible (R): VP Marketing / Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1558_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1558_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1558_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1558_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1558_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-282 (ensure controlled execution — Digital Marketing &amp; Social Media (PA-14.2).) | - operational: allowing honest product reviews and not script-approving every word
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1558_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1558_Annotation12" targetRef="W1558_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
