    <bpmn:process id="W_W1559" name="W1559. Localized Geo-Targeted Digital Advertising for Store-Level Promotions &amp; Event Traffic Driving" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store-specific promotional event (sale weekend, vendor demo day per W1379, workshop per W147, grand opening per W1444); or monthly local promotion calendar; or store manager request for local traffic boost
Frequency: Ongoing; ~200 stores × 2–4 local campaigns/month = ~400–800 local campaigns/month
Volume: Each campaign targets 30,000–100,000 people within store catchment area; total monthly reach: ~20–40M impressions across all stores
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager
Participants: Digital Marketing Manager, Store Manager, Category Manager, Marketing Campaign Manager, External Media Agency
Source: workflow W1559 — Localized Geo-Targeted Digital Advertising for Store-Level Promotions &amp; Event Traffic Driving</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1559_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1559_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1559_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1559_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1559_Lane2" name="Digital Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1559_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1559_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1559_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1559_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1559_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1559_Start4" name="Store-specific promotional event (sale weekend, vendor demo day per W1379, workshop per…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1559_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1559_Task5" name="Campaign trigger &amp; brief">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Campaign trigger &amp; brief: Store Manager or Category Manager submits local campaign request: (a) what: event/promotion details (dates, products, offers), (b) where: target store(s) and geographic radius, (c) who: target audience (DIY homeowners, trade pros, or both), (d) budget: PHP 5,000–50,000 per campaign depending on event scale; (e) Digital Marketing Manager reviews and approves budget allocation
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Category Manager / Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 15–30 min/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1559_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1559_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1559_Task6" name="Geo-targeted ad creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Geo-targeted ad creation: Digital Marketing Manager or External Media Agency creates localized ad creative: (a) ad formats: (i) Facebook/Instagram carousel ad featuring 3–5 promotional products with store-specific pricing, (ii) Google Ads search campaign for &quot;[product] [city name]&quot; keywords (e.g., &quot;cement Davao price&quot;), (iii) Facebook event promotion for in-store events (demo day, workshop), (iv) SMS blast to loyalty members in store catchment per W1350; (b) targeting parameters: (i) geo-fence: radius around target store (5 km for urban, 15 km for provincial), (ii) audience: BuildRight loyalty members in area + lookalike audiences + interest-based (home improvement, construction, DIY), (iii) demographics: age 25–60, split by trade pro vs. retail customer segments per W1452
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Media Agency
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1–2 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1559_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1559_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1559_Task7" name="Campaign execution &amp; monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Campaign execution &amp; monitoring: (a) launch campaign with daily budget pacing (PHP 1,000–10,000/day depending on campaign); (b) monitor daily: impressions, reach, click-through rate, cost per click, and conversions (online clicks to buildright.com.ph, promo code redemptions, store visits via location data); (c) optimize mid-campaign: reallocate budget to best-performing ad sets, pause underperforming creatives, adjust targeting if reach is insufficient
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Media Agency
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–30 min/day during campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1559_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1559_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1559_Task8" name="Store-level attribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Store-level attribution: (a) post-campaign: Digital Marketing Manager compiles store-level campaign report: (i) total reach and impressions within geo-fence, (ii) click-through rate vs. benchmark (target: &gt; 2% for Facebook, &gt; 5% for Google), (iii) estimated store visits (via location data from mobile devices — Facebook/Google store visit attribution), (iv) sales impact: compare event/promotion day sales vs. baseline (average of prior 4 weekends); (b) share report with Store Manager and Category Manager for promotional effectiveness assessment
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Data Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1 hour/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1559_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1559_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1559_Task9" name="Monthly local advertising optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly local advertising optimization: Digital Marketing Manager reviews all local campaigns monthly: (a) aggregate performance by store region, campaign type, and channel; (b) identify high-performing stores (local campaigns drive &gt; 20% sales lift) and low-performing stores (&lt; 5% lift); (c) optimize: (i) increase budget for high-performing store campaigns, (ii) adjust targeting or creative for low-performing stores, (iii) identify seasonal patterns (certain regions respond better during specific periods); (d) update local advertising playbook: best practices, top-performing ad formats, optimal geo-radius by market type
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1559_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1559_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1559_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1559_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1559_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-282 (ensure controlled execution — Digital Marketing &amp; Social Media (PA-14.2).) | - operational: template-based creative production with store-specific localization (store name, address, local pricing); operational: comparing ad-driven metrics against store baseline
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1559_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1559_Annotation11" targetRef="W1559_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
