    <bpmn:process id="W_W1560" name="W1560. Customer Review &amp; User-Generated Content Management, Online Reputation Monitoring &amp; Response" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New customer review posted on Google Business, Facebook, TripAdvisor, or buildright.com.ph; or weekly reputation monitoring cycle; or negative review alert trigger
Frequency: ~200–400 new reviews/month across all platforms for 200 store locations + national brand pages; weekly monitoring cycle; real-time negative review alerts
Volume: ~2,400–4,800 reviews/year; average 3.8–4.2 star rating target; ~5–10% negative reviews (1–2 stars) requiring response
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager
Participants: Digital Marketing Manager, Customer Service Manager, Store Manager (for store-specific reviews), VP Marketing, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1560 — Customer Review &amp; User-Generated Content Management, Online Reputation Monitoring &amp; Response</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1560_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1560_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1560_Lane2" name="Digital Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1560_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1560_Start4" name="New customer review posted on Google Business, Facebook, TripAdvisor, or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1560_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1560_Task5" name="Real-time review monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Real-time review monitoring: System monitors all 200 store Google Business Profiles, BuildRight Facebook Page, and buildright.com.ph product reviews: (a) new review notifications pushed to Digital Marketing Manager dashboard; (b) sentiment classification: positive (4–5 stars), neutral (3 stars), negative (1–2 stars); (c) negative review alert: real-time SMS/email to Digital Marketing Manager and relevant Store Manager for reviews &lt; 3 stars; (d) weekly: compile review summary by store, region, and chain-wide
Responsible (R): System / Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated + 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1560_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1560_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1560_Task6" name="Negative review response &amp; service recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Negative review response &amp; service recovery: For negative reviews (1–2 stars): (a) Digital Marketing Manager drafts public response within 24 hours: (i) acknowledge the customer&#x27;s experience, (ii) apologize sincerely, (iii) invite the customer to contact Customer Service Manager directly (provide email/phone), (iv) assure the customer that the issue will be addressed; (b) simultaneously: Store Manager investigates the incident — review internal records (POS transaction, staffing, incident reports per W140) and speaks with involved staff; (c) Customer Service Manager contacts the reviewer privately (if contact information available): (i) understand the full situation, (ii) offer resolution (refund, replacement, discount on next visit, loyalty points credit), (iii) request review update if resolved to customer&#x27;s satisfaction; (d) resolution logged in CRM per W41 for pattern tracking
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Store Manager / Customer Service Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 30–60 min per negative review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1560_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1560_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1560_Task7" name="Positive review engagement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Positive review engagement: For positive reviews (4–5 stars): (a) Digital Marketing Manager or system auto-responds with: (i) thank the customer by name, (ii) highlight the specific positive aspect mentioned, (iii) invite the customer to the next workshop or promotion; (b) monthly: identify the top 5 most enthusiastic reviewers per store — consider for loyalty program upgrade or brand ambassador per W1561
Responsible (R): System / Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated + 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1560_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1560_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1560_Task8" name="Review generation program">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Review generation program: Proactively encourage satisfied customers to leave reviews: (a) post-purchase email/SMS per W1350: &quot;How was your experience at BuildRight [store name]? Leave a review and earn 50 bonus loyalty points!&quot;; (b) in-store: Customer Service Counter displays &quot;Review us on Google/Facebook&quot; signage with QR code; (c) post-workshop per W147: &quot;Enjoyed the workshop? Share your experience on Facebook and tag BuildRight!&quot;; (d) target: increase average reviews per store per month from ~1–2 to ~5–10; (e) quarterly incentive: stores with highest review volume and average rating &gt; 4.2 recognized in store operations review per W575
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1560_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1560_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1560_Task9" name="User-generated content (UGC) harvesting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: User-generated content (UGC) harvesting: Identify and leverage customer-generated project content: (a) monitor social media for BuildRight mentions, tags, and hashtags (#BuildRightProject, #BuildRightDepot); (b) for standout customer projects (beautiful tile installation, impressive deck build, creative furniture project): (i) request permission to feature on BuildRight&#x27;s social media per W142, (ii) create &quot;Customer Spotlight&quot; post with before/after photos and customer quote, (iii) offer PHP 1,000 gift card as thank-you for featured UGC; (c) quarterly: compile UGC gallery for buildright.com.ph &quot;Project Inspiration&quot; section and in-store display screens
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Content Creator
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1560_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1560_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1560_Task10" name="Monthly reputation analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly reputation analytics: Digital Marketing Manager produces monthly online reputation report: (a) average star rating by store, region, and chain-wide; (b) review volume trend; (c) sentiment analysis: common themes in positive reviews (friendly staff, wide selection) and negative reviews (stockouts, long queues, pricing errors); (d) negative review resolution rate: % of negative reviews that received response within 24 hours and were resolved; (e) competitive benchmark: BuildRight average rating vs. competitor hardware/home improvement retailers in Philippines; (f) action items: specific stores needing reputation improvement, recurring issues requiring operational fixes
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Data Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1560_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1560_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1560_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1560_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1560_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-282 (ensure controlled execution — Digital Marketing &amp; Social Media (PA-14.2).) | - operational: Digital Marketing Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Digital Marketing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
