    <bpmn:process id="W_W5568" name="W5568. Official-Channel Account-Takeover Response (Brand-Account Hijack)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: BuildRight&#x27;s own official social-media pages, messaging channels (Viber/WhatsApp/Messenger), marketplace seller accounts or app-store listings are compromised — scam promotions, fake giveaways or phishing links posted from the genuine verified account, admin access lost to a hijacker, anomalous admin logins flagged, or followers reporting fraud content that carries BuildRight&#x27;s real handle
Frequency: Rare; ~0–2 confirmed takeover attempts per year across the official channel estate (the verified accounts are high-value targets precisely because their scam posts inherit platform trust)
Volume: 1 takeover × the hijacked account&#x27;s follower base (the largest page reaches ~2.1M followers) × every follower who sees the fraud post before takedown — the blast radius is trust, not inventory
Owner: Social Media Manager (channel recovery); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (fraud-content posture)
Participants: Digital Marketing Manager (channel program), IT Security (credential forensics, W383/W5518), VS-27.3 (access &amp; infrastructure containment), platform trust-&amp;-safety channels (recovery appeals), VS-13/VS-07 (inbound customer-inquiry scripts), VS-14.3 (crisis comms per W134/W855 ring), VS-91 (data exposure where follower DMs or records are accessible), W5563 (the fake-page sibling canon for any copycat waves riding the confusion)
Source: workflow W5568 — Official-Channel Account-Takeover Response (Brand-Account Hijack)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5568_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5568_Lane1" name="Social Media Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5568_Lane2" name="IT Security">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5568_Lane3" name="VS-14.3">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5568_Lane4" name="VS-13">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5568_Lane5" name="VS-91">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5568_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5568_Start7" name="BuildRight&#x27;s own official social-media pages, messaging channels…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5568_Task8" name="Contain the credential">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Contain the credential: force password/reset and revoke sessions and API tokens for the affected account and every admin sharing the credential; suspend scheduled-post queues so stale promo content cannot fire mid-incident
Responsible (R): Social Media Manager / IT Security
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: First hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5568_Task9" name="Evidence &amp; scope">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Evidence &amp; scope: capture the fraud posts, timestamps and reach before takedown; IT Security establishes the entry vector (phished admin, reused password, third-party tool token) and whether any other channel or mailbox shares the compromise (W383/W5518)
Responsible (R): IT Security / Social Media Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5568_Task10" name="Platform recovery appeal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Platform recovery appeal: engage the platform&#x27;s verified-account/compromised-business channels with corporate proof (SEC records, domain control, ad-account history); request fraud-post removal and admin restoration — the appeal rides the platform relationship, never paid &quot;recovery services&quot;
Responsible (R): Social Media Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5568_Task11" name="Follower advisory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Follower advisory: same-day advisory from unaffected official channels — the hijacked account is compromised, BuildRight never runs pay-to-claim giveaways or e-wallet-only promos, and the website/app are the transaction surface of record; service desks get the inquiry script
Responsible (R): VS-14.3 / Brand
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5568_Task12" name="Victim &amp; fraud watch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Victim &amp; fraud watch: followers who interacted with the fraud post get the W5563-class guidance (platform report channel, e-wallet/bank recall request, PNP Anti-Cybercrime referral); VS-125/VS-13 watch for presentment abuse and complaint spikes
Responsible (R): VS-13 / VS-125
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Event-long</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5568_Task13" name="Privacy assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Privacy assessment: where the hijacker could access follower messages or audience data, route the VS-91 assessment — the W53 NPC clock applies from confirmation of unauthorized access
Responsible (R): VS-91 / DPO
Accountable (A): Data Protection Officer
Duration: Per W53</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5568_Task14" name="Restore &amp; harden">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Restore &amp; harden: admin restoration verified against the role roster; hardware-token/2FA mandatory on the channel estate; third-party posting-tool tokens rotated; the W5563 fake-page watch tuned for copycats riding the incident
Responsible (R): Social Media Manager / IT Security
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5568_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5568_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5568_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5568_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-282 (ensure controlled execution — Digital Marketing &amp; Social Media (PA-14.2).) | - operational: official-channel admin access is 2FA-protected with a named-role roster; takeover containment (credential revocation and queue freeze) executes within the first hour of confirmation; follower advisories run only from unaffected verified channels
Owner: Social Media Manager (channel recovery); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (fraud-content posture)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5568_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5568_Annotation16" targetRef="W5568_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
